              SSIIGGSSTTKKSSZZ  is  defined to be large enough to cover the usual size
              requirements for an alternate signal  stack,  and  the  constant
              MMIINNSSIIGGSSTTKKSSZZ  defines the minimum size required to execute a sig‐
              nal handler.

       To disable an existing stack, specify _s_s_._s_s___f_l_a_g_s  as  SSSS__DDIISSAABBLLEE.   In
       this  case,  the  kernel ignores any other flags in _s_s_._s_s___f_l_a_g_s and the
       remaining fields in _s_s.

       If _o_l_d___s_s is not NULL, then it is used to return information about  the
       alternate signal stack which was in effect prior to the call to ssiiggaalltt‐‐
       ssttaacckk().   The _o_l_d___s_s_._s_s___s_p and _o_l_d___s_s_._s_s___s_i_z_e fields return the start‐
